# Squares and Cubes Practice

Complete the table below by calculating the missing values[cite: 9]. Use your knowledge of perfect squares (up to 20) and perfect cubes (up to 15) to find the base numbers and their powers[cite: 9].

> **Remember:**
> - To find a Square ($n^2$), multiply the base by itself: $n \times n$[cite: 9].
> - To find a Cube ($n^3$), multiply the base by itself three times: $n \times n \times n$[cite: 9].

